cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use autocode, please cite it as below."
title: "AutoCode: 11 agent skills from a spoken request, or a product you admire, to a deployed URL"
abstract: >-
  AutoCode is a skill pack that takes a plain-language request through building,
  testing and deployment in a single session and returns a live URL. Say "I want
  something like X" and its product-study skill studies X from public pages
  only, writes a blueprint in which every line carries its source and a
  confidence level, cuts an MVP small enough to build in one session, and builds
  it, learning the structure while designing its own look. One command, python3
  autocode.py setup (Python 3.8+, no dependencies), detects the coding agents on
  the machine and installs the 11 skills and a managed persona block into any of
  them, including Claude Code, Codex, Hermes, OpenCode, Gemini CLI, Cursor,
  Windsurf, Trae, CodeBuddy, Qwen Code and OpenClaw; doctor and uninstall leave
  the user's own edits intact. AutoCode uses the iLang v5.0 judgment layer to
  decide when to stop and ask, keeps deployment secrets out of the model
  context, and ships a release gate that checks every manifest, version and
  installer scenario before a release.
